ve 3 along with J7, and forces a Black response. With a Live 3 it will set a "Four" for next turn.\nThe alternative was H11.\n\nWhile I checked for a more complex 4-3 combination, no options popped out. K8, seems to create a Live 3 that is a strong, safe starting position. There is also an open 2 at J7-K8. It forces a Black response. While not a guaranteed win, a strong move with a very sound foundation.\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation: The current board shows White with several clusters of stones, but no immediate 4-in-a-row threats. Black has some stones but their major diagonal threat (F6-I9) is blocked at both ends. White has a strong "Sleeping Three" formation on the anti-diagonal with stones at I10 and J9. Extending this line is the most promising strategy.\n\nReason: By playing at K8, White extends the I10-J9 line to form a "Live Three" (Open 3) consisting of I10-J9-K8. This formation is open at both ends (H11 and L7), forcing Black to block one end, which gives White the initiative. Additionally, placing a stone at K8 connects diagonally with the existing White stone at J7, creating further tactical opportunities.\n\nAnswer: {"col": "K", "row": 8}'}
